2026-09-06  David Walther  <david@clearbrookdistillery.com>

	* filsys_ops.h, check.c, v7fs.c, v1fs.c, pdp7fs.c, filsys.c: fold the
	*_op wrapper layer.  The ops vtable now takes filsys_edition_t * (not
	void *) -- every backend already aliases that type -- so the ~66 one-line
	void*-to-typed adapters are deleted and the tables point at the real
	functions directly.  The *_op functions that remain carry real logic
	(blocksize, check, max_file, statfs), not a signature cast.

2026-09-06  David Walther  <david@clearbrookdistillery.com>

	* test_matrix.c, filsys_format.c: drive the per-format regression table
	from the shared edition table too.  The direct-block capacity and the max
	file size now derive from the descriptor (ndaddr * bsize, ops->max_file)
	and the mkfs block count is a test default, so a new edition is exercised
	with no hand-written row; PDP-7's descriptor gains ndaddr.

2026-09-06  David Walther  <david@clearbrookdistillery.com>

	* mkfs.filsys.c, v7fs.c: fold mkfs's parallel per-format layout paths
	into one descriptor-driven driver.  The free-list-cache editions
	(V7/32V/Coherent/Xenix/2.9BSD/V6/2.11BSD) now build a filesystem through
	the library's ops/alloc vtable -- alloc_ops for balloc/bfree, write_inode
	for the on-disk inode codec, and the check driver's makefree for the
	per-edition interleave -- leaving only the i-list sizing and the seed
	(reserved + root) inodes as per-format hooks.  bsd211 gains a makefree
	(sequential salvage).  V1 and PDP-7 stay their own paths.

2026-09-06  David Walther  <david@clearbrookdistillery.com>

	* v7fs.c, v7fs.h, filsys_format.c: fold V6 into the V7 engine.  The
	allocator (balloc/bfree/ialloc/ifree), the superblock open/sync/write,
	and the check-driver seams (mark_block, walk_free, maxino/data_start/
	data_end, is_clean, statfs) become one shared implementation driven by
	two new descriptor fields -- daddr_wid (2-byte V6 vs 4-byte V7 block
	addresses) and isize_count (s_isize as i-list block count vs first data
	block) -- plus the v7_data_first/v7_maxinode/v7_get_daddr/v7_put_daddr
	helpers.  Only the ILARG bmap topology, the 32-byte inode codec, and the
	mode-specific checker pieces remain V6-specific.
	* filsys_format.c, filsys.h, mkfs.filsys.c, fsck.filsys.c,
	mount.filsys.c, test_matrix.c: single-source the edition name/alias table
	in filsys_format.c (filsys_format_nth, filsys_edition_by_name,
	filsys_editions_usage); the tools resolve -v and generate their usage
	lines through it instead of four hand-maintained parse_edition chains,
	and test_matrix's namelength iterates it so PDP-7 is covered.

